# Copy to a file of your own and `source` it before scripts/design/webdev.sh, or
# set these inline.
#
#   set -a; . scripts/design/webdev.env.example; set +a; scripts/design/webdev.sh
#
# Commented lines are the reference run's values. Uncommenting one at a different
# value changes the experiment, not just the run. The music arm has its own file
# rather than a section here, because the two arms disagree on several of these
# names -- a shared file would let the wrong arm's value win silently.

# Two modes, and they are not interchangeable. Training's reward is the rank of a
# rollout against its own GRPO siblings, so a single number from it means nothing
# on its own; evaluation renders in the pod and scores absolutely.
# WEBDEV_MODE=train

# --- required in both modes -------------------------------------------------
# Policy checkpoint; this model line wants the mm-wrapped build.
MODEL_PATH=/path/to/policy-checkpoint
# Build these first:
#   python3 -m recipes.design.webdev.build_parquet --input <tasks>.parquet --output <out>.parquet
TRAIN_DATA=/path/to/webdev_train.parquet
VAL_DATA=/path/to/webdev_train.parquet
# Able to create sandbox pods -- one per trajectory.
KUBECONFIG=/path/to/kubeconfig
# Egress proxy chain the in-pod browser uses to reach public CDNs. Without it the
# agent's externally referenced images render broken and the judge scores the page
# down for placeholder assets. Comma-separated failover chain; a trailing comma
# appends a direct attempt.
POD_PROXY=http://proxy-a:3128,http://proxy-b:3128,
#
# Trajectory dumps, and on the training path the screenshots the group pick
# compares. **It must be a filesystem shared by the workers AND the driver**: the
# pod's actor writes them and the driver reads them back by path. Node-local,
# every group comes back too small to judge and every reward stays 0.0 with no
# error anywhere. Watch webdev_group/n_groups_too_small.
WEBDEV_DEBUG_DIR=/shared/disk/webdev_dumps

# --- required for WEBDEV_MODE=train -----------------------------------------
# A group-capable grading service. run_webdev.sh handshakes it before launching,
# and checks capabilities rather than a version string -- pinning a version and
# then upgrading the service made every training retry fatal in the handshake.
DESIGN_GRADER_URL=http://grader-host:8000
# That service's own judge auth. Missing, every reward drops to 0.
LLM_JUDGE_API_KEY=

# --- required for WEBDEV_MODE=eval ------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible vision endpoint. The model is named explicitly on
# purpose: there is no default, because a run judged by a different model than the
# numbers it will be compared against is worse than one that refuses to start.
# WEBDEV_EVAL_JUDGE_BASE_URL=
# WEBDEV_EVAL_JUDGE_API_KEY=
# WEBDEV_EVAL_JUDGE_MODEL=

# --- cluster ----------------------------------------------------------------
# TRAIN_NNODES=8
# TRAIN_NGPUS_PER_NODE=8
# ACTOR_TP=8
# ACTOR_PP=1
# ACTOR_CP=1
# ROLLOUT_TP=4
# AGENT_NUM_WORKERS=32

# --- rollout ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A build trajectory is dozens of turns of tool output, so nearly the whole
# window is response budget: 262144 - 16384 = 245760.
# MAXLEN=262144
# PROMPT_LENGTH=16384
# N=8
# TRAIN_BATCH_SIZE=32
# prompt-mean computes its weights over a whole optimizer batch, so the sampling
# batch must be exactly one minibatch. run_webdev.sh refuses to launch otherwise.
# PPO_MINI_BATCH_SIZE=32
# TOTAL_EPOCHS=1
# ROLLOUT_GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.75
# ROLLOUT_MAX_RUNNING_REQUESTS=64
#
# Measured, not inherited: a run that passed these three scored 0.56 at step 1
# while runs that left verl's naked defaults sat at 0.26-0.36 on the same
# checkpoint, data and grader weights. The lower temperature costs no exploration
# -- in-group variance was unchanged.
# ROLLOUT_TEMPERATURE=0.6
# ROLLOUT_TOP_P=0.95
# ROLLOUT_TOP_K=20

# --- agent loop budgets -----------------------------------------------------
# 0 means no wall. Under partial rollout a trajectory's wall clock includes every
# training window it sleeps through, so a cap culls healthy long trajectories
# rather than stuck ones. MimoAgent's own pod timeout is the backstop.
# TRAJECTORY_TIMEOUT=0
# ENV_SETUP_TIMEOUT=900
# REWARD_TIMEOUT=1500
# The environment actor holds a pod and waits on it; it does not compute, so a
# whole CPU each would cap concurrency on an accounting number.
# ENV_NUM_CPUS=0.125
# Both off. The first kills the job on the first pod that fails to come up; the
# second writes an out-of-range sentinel that upstream GRPO would optimise against.
# FAIL_ON_ENV_SETUP_ERROR=False
# INVALID_REWARD_FOR_INFRA=False

# --- grading ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Serve the deliverable over loopback http rather than file://. Not optional in
# practice: browsers block module loading, fetch and XHR on the file protocol, so
# a React, Vue or ES-module site renders as an empty body however good it is --
# measured at 44 of 182 shots blank, and React is named in 30% of the briefs.
# Scores across this boundary are NOT comparable.
# WEBDEV_GRADE_HTTP=1
# Exclude infra-failed rollouts from their GRPO group. Left in, a pod that never
# came up scores 0.0, drags the group mean down and hands every sibling a spurious
# positive advantage.
# DROP_INFRA_FROM_GROUP=1

# --- identity ---------------------------------------------------------------
# SAVE_FREQ=10
# PROJECT_NAME=opensource-design
